# Spec-Driven Development

- Read `.specify/memory/constitution.md` before changing gameplay.
- Read `docs/GAME_DESIGN.md` before changing fantasy, cameras, weapons, loot look, or tone. The bible wins on who you are; the constitution wins on engineering.
- New behavior starts as a spec under `specs/`, then plan, then tasks. Do not invent large features only in code.
- Use the numbered feature branch. Do not commit feature work to `main`.
- Implementation follows `tasks.md` in order: Setup → Foundation → stories. Stop at a story checkpoint and play it.
- Simulation (shotgun, slash, execute, waves, reset) must stay testable without WebGL.
- If a change does not make the Demolisher feel more unstoppable, it does not belong.
